1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,710
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:04,960
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,110
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:07,020
I had my right knee

5
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:08,680
replaced two years ago.

6
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:10,480
It has hurt every day
since.

7
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:11,820
Not surgery pain.

8
00:00:11,820 --> 00:00:12,990
I know what that felt
like,

9
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:13,810
and it went away.

10
00:00:13,810 --> 00:00:15,120
This is different.

11
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:15,930
Tight.

12
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:16,810
Full.

13
00:00:16,810 --> 00:00:17,710
Like a band around

14
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:19,500
the joint that never
loosens.

15
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:20,700
And for two years

16
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:22,300
I've been told the same
thing.

17
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:23,440
Give it time.

18
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,900
At six weeks it was
swelling,

19
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:26,190
and swelling is normal.

20
00:00:26,190 --> 00:00:27,200
At three months,

21
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,340
give it six.

22
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:29,060
At six months,

23
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:30,680
some knees take a full
year.

24
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:31,360
At a year,

25
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:33,750
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

26
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:35,310
And I didn't just wait.

27
00:00:35,310 --> 00:00:36,880
We went down the list.

28
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:38,270
More physical therapy.

29
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:39,130
Every session,

30
00:00:39,130 --> 00:00:40,780
every exercise at home.

31
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:41,970
I got stronger.

32
00:00:41,970 --> 00:00:43,620
The tightness never moved.

33
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:44,940
The pain pills helped,

34
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:46,350
and that was the problem.

35
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:48,300
I'm already on enough
every morning,

36
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:49,270
and nobody could tell me

37
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:50,800
when I'd get to stop.

38
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,020
Then a nerve block.

39
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:53,720
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

40
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,020
And after that, a second

41
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:56,100
operation to go back

42
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:57,700
in and do it over.

43
00:00:57,700 --> 00:00:59,140
I said no.

44
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:00,850
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

45
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:02,010
and my knee felt like

46
00:01:02,010 --> 00:01:03,740
a band was wrapped around
it,

47
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:06,360
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

48
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:07,730
Every morning I took
something

49
00:01:07,730 --> 00:01:08,760
for it and got

50
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:09,990
on with my day.

51
00:01:09,990 --> 00:01:11,560
Couldn't do the stairs,

52
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:12,630
couldn't stand at the
counter

53
00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:14,190
long enough to finish
dinner,

54
00:01:14,190 --> 00:01:15,710
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

55
00:01:15,710 --> 00:01:18,070
game without shifting
every two minutes.

56
00:01:18,070 --> 00:01:19,550
It woke me at night,

57
00:01:19,550 --> 00:01:21,910
and it turned ordinary
things,

58
00:01:21,910 --> 00:01:23,540
like getting in the car

59
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:25,080
or up off the couch,

60
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:26,240
into a decision.

61
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:27,530
After a long and serious

62
00:01:27,530 --> 00:01:28,850
talk with my wife,

63
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:31,060
I went back in one more
time.

64
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:32,220
That was the fourth set

65
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:34,100
of X-rays on this knee.

66
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:35,790
And like the three before
it,

67
00:01:35,790 --> 00:01:38,240
the answer was everything
looks great.

68
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:39,960
No loosening, no
infection,

69
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:40,970
nothing wrong.

70
00:01:40,970 --> 00:01:41,820
Only this time there

71
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:43,220
was no new number.

72
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:44,280
Nobody said

73
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,550
give it another six
months.

74
00:01:45,550 --> 00:01:47,410
There was nothing left to
give it.

75
00:01:47,410 --> 00:01:48,220
I sat in the parking

76
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:49,450
lot for a while.

77
00:01:49,450 --> 00:01:50,980
Okay, I thought.

78
00:01:50,980 --> 00:01:52,560
Then explain this.

79
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:54,440
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

80
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:55,950
I hit my breaking point.

81
00:01:55,950 --> 00:01:58,010
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

82
00:01:58,010 --> 00:01:59,810
Everyone in the house was
asleep

83
00:01:59,810 --> 00:02:01,540
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

84
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:02,750
with my leg up,

85
00:02:02,750 --> 00:02:04,250
trying to find any angle
where

86
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:05,360
it didn't feel like
something

87
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:06,810
was wrapped around my knee

88
00:02:06,810 --> 00:02:07,850
and tightening.

89
00:02:07,850 --> 00:02:10,250
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

90
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:12,390
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

91
00:02:12,390 --> 00:02:13,350
And I just thought,

92
00:02:13,350 --> 00:02:15,140
is this really my life
now?

93
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:16,880
I can't live like this.

94
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:18,770
So I made myself a
promise.

95
00:02:18,770 --> 00:02:19,620
I wouldn't go a day

96
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:21,430
without looking for an
answer.

97
00:02:21,430 --> 00:02:23,000
And when I found one,

98
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,880
I'd share it with everyone

99
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:26,770
going through the same
thing.

100
00:02:26,770 --> 00:02:27,870
So I got my laptop

101
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:29,780
out and went looking.

102
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:31,120
Not for a product.

103
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,650
For an explanation.

104
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:34,330
Mayo Clinic forums,

105
00:02:34,330 --> 00:02:36,440
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

106
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:39,080
doctor videos, medical
animations.

107
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:40,020
And that's when I found

108
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:41,810
a video from a physical
therapist

109
00:02:41,810 --> 00:02:42,340
named Dr.

110
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:44,350
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

111
00:02:44,350 --> 00:02:46,310
had been through exactly
this.

112
00:02:46,310 --> 00:02:48,560
But before I say anything
else,

113
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:50,360
I want to be straight with
you.

114
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:52,750
You've already had
something work fast.

115
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:53,700
The ice.

116
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:55,330
The first week of a new
pill.

117
00:02:55,330 --> 00:02:57,250
The good day after a
session.

118
00:02:57,250 --> 00:02:58,350
Then it wore off.

119
00:02:58,350 --> 00:03:00,910
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

120
00:03:00,910 --> 00:03:03,030
Fast relief isn't relief.

121
00:03:03,030 --> 00:03:04,330
It's a preview.

122
00:03:04,330 --> 00:03:05,350
So I'm not going to tell

123
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:06,800
you this works fast.

124
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:07,970
It doesn't.

125
00:03:07,970 --> 00:03:09,840
But if you're willing to
be patient,

126
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:10,560
and to look at what's

127
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:11,850
going on around your new
knee

128
00:03:11,850 --> 00:03:13,450
instead of inside it,
there

129
00:03:13,450 --> 00:03:15,660
is a real reason it still
hurts.

130
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:17,970
And something you can do
about it.

131
00:03:17,970 --> 00:03:19,270
Let me explain what he
said,

132
00:03:19,270 --> 00:03:20,700
because this is what
changed

133
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:22,130
everything for me.

134
00:03:22,130 --> 00:03:24,220
He started with the
basics.

135
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:25,720
A knee replacement takes
out

136
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:27,460
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

137
00:03:27,460 --> 00:03:28,870
in metal and plastic.

138
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:30,900
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

139
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:32,700
you had before the
operation.

140
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:34,360
That part I already knew.

141
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:35,700
But then he explained
something

142
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:37,070
nobody had ever told me.

143
00:03:37,070 --> 00:03:37,890
He said,

144
00:03:37,890 --> 00:03:39,570
think about a swollen foot

145
00:03:39,570 --> 00:03:41,260
inside a shoe.

146
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:42,670
The shoe didn't shrink.

147
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:44,850
Your foot is taking up
more room,

148
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:46,300
so everything feels
cramped

149
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:47,900
and tight and squeezed.

150
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:48,790
Your new knee sits

151
00:03:48,790 --> 00:03:50,290
in a limited space with
living

152
00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:52,330
tissue packed all around
it.

153
00:03:52,330 --> 00:03:54,190
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

154
00:03:54,190 --> 00:03:56,010
had to work through that
tissue.

155
00:03:56,010 --> 00:03:58,890
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

156
00:03:58,890 --> 00:04:00,450
At first that's normal.

157
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:02,030
But in some people that
swelling can

158
00:04:02,030 --> 00:04:04,810
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

159
00:04:04,810 --> 00:04:06,670
And swollen tissue takes
up more

160
00:04:06,670 --> 00:04:08,620
room than calm tissue
does.

161
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:09,980
So when you bend,

162
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:11,900
that tissue gets
compressed.

163
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:13,070
When you straighten,

164
00:04:13,070 --> 00:04:14,640
it gets pulled tight.

165
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:15,840
That's the band.

166
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:18,250
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

167
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:19,210
And you start being

168
00:04:19,210 --> 00:04:20,320
the one who says,

169
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:21,200
you go ahead.

170
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,560
I'll stay here.

171
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:24,390
And that's exactly why so
much

172
00:04:24,390 --> 00:04:26,770
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

173
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:28,920
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

174
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:29,980
around the knee.

175
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:30,970
Worth doing,

176
00:04:30,970 --> 00:04:31,960
and I'd done it.

177
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:33,320
It does nothing about
tissue

178
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:34,610
taking up room.

179
00:04:34,610 --> 00:04:36,100
A nerve block quiets

180
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:38,580
the nerve carrying the
signal.

181
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:40,680
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

182
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:42,300
But when that irritated
tissue

183
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:43,910
finally calms down,

184
00:04:43,910 --> 00:04:45,370
it holds less fluid,

185
00:04:45,370 --> 00:04:47,010
and it takes up less room.

186
00:04:47,010 --> 00:04:48,350
Less room taken up means

187
00:04:48,350 --> 00:04:50,500
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

188
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,670
That's what takes the
pressure off.

189
00:04:52,670 --> 00:04:54,160
After two years of this,

190
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:56,110
it finally made sense.

191
00:04:56,110 --> 00:04:58,140
The problem was never the
new knee.

192
00:04:58,140 --> 00:05:00,400
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

193
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,010
He calls it the squeeze.

194
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:04,710
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

195
00:05:04,710 --> 00:05:06,190
I'd bought knee sleeves,

196
00:05:06,190 --> 00:05:08,460
compression braces,
creams,

197
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:10,280
half of Amazon really,

198
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:11,680
and all any of it gave me

199
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:12,910
was an hour.

200
00:05:12,910 --> 00:05:13,990
I even looked at going

201
00:05:13,990 --> 00:05:15,930
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

202
00:05:15,930 --> 00:05:18,010
But at $200 a session

203
00:05:18,010 --> 00:05:19,800
with nothing covered by
insurance,

204
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:21,140
that was a quick no.

205
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:22,250
Then one night I went

206
00:05:22,250 --> 00:05:23,520
back to that knee
replacement

207
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:25,250
group and actually read
it.

208
00:05:25,250 --> 00:05:26,580
Thousands of people,

209
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:28,200
years out from surgery,

210
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:30,500
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

211
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,220
nobody could explain.

212
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:33,950
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

213
00:05:33,950 --> 00:05:35,760
the same thing kept coming
up.

214
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:37,740
This one device,

215
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:39,240
and people saying it was
the first

216
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:40,940
thing that made a
difference.

217
00:05:40,940 --> 00:05:43,120
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

218
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:44,440
alright, here it comes,

219
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:45,790
he's selling me something,

220
00:05:45,790 --> 00:05:47,620
let me shut that down
right now.

221
00:05:47,620 --> 00:05:49,110
I'm only here because I
made myself

222
00:05:49,110 --> 00:05:51,100
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

223
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,050
that if I ever found

224
00:05:52,050 --> 00:05:53,170
something that helped,

225
00:05:53,170 --> 00:05:54,780
I'd say so.

226
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:56,550
It's called the KenRelief
Red

227
00:05:56,550 --> 00:05:58,170
Light Therapy Wrap.

228
00:05:58,170 --> 00:06:00,260
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

229
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:01,370
It looked like the cheap

230
00:06:01,370 --> 00:06:03,150
knee sleeves off Amazon

231
00:06:03,150 --> 00:06:04,790
that did nothing for me.

232
00:06:04,790 --> 00:06:06,860
But I went to their
website anyway,

233
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:07,760
just to see what all

234
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:09,150
the fuss was about.

235
00:06:09,150 --> 00:06:10,760
It's the same red light
therapy

236
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:12,970
clinics charge $200 a
session

237
00:06:12,970 --> 00:06:15,250
for, off machines that
cost

238
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:16,830
fifty thousand dollars,

239
00:06:16,830 --> 00:06:17,800
in a wrap you plug

240
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,340
into the wall at home.

241
00:06:19,340 --> 00:06:21,190
Two hundred and forty
lights.

242
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:23,110
Red at 660 nanometers

243
00:06:23,110 --> 00:06:25,460
and near-infrared at 850,

244
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:28,020
run together for the
strongest effect.

245
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:29,510
Four strength levels.

246
00:06:29,510 --> 00:06:31,860
A five to thirty minute
timer.

247
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:33,840
Then I saw the guarantee.

248
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:35,440
Ninety days.

249
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:37,910
Results or your money
back,

250
00:06:37,910 --> 00:06:40,510
no questions, no store
credit,

251
00:06:40,510 --> 00:06:42,670
and you don't even send it
back.

252
00:06:42,670 --> 00:06:45,060
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

253
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:46,720
days to change my mind.

254
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:48,010
There wasn't much to lose,

255
00:06:48,010 --> 00:06:49,510
so I ordered it.

256
00:06:49,510 --> 00:06:51,170
Two of them, actually.

257
00:06:51,170 --> 00:06:53,080
Only the right knee was
replaced,

258
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:55,320
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

259
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:57,270
and I'd done it for two
years.

260
00:06:57,270 --> 00:06:59,440
The left one was carrying
the difference.

261
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,370
When it came,

262
00:07:00,370 --> 00:07:02,570
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

263
00:07:02,570 --> 00:07:03,930
because I'd been let down
too

264
00:07:03,930 --> 00:07:05,770
many times to get excited.

265
00:07:05,770 --> 00:07:07,450
What I felt was warmth.

266
00:07:07,450 --> 00:07:09,660
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

267
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:11,710
More like it was coming
from inside

268
00:07:11,710 --> 00:07:14,040
the knee and spreading
around it.

269
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,260
And that was it.

270
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:16,990
That was the whole
experience.

271
00:07:16,990 --> 00:07:17,990
When I took it off,

272
00:07:17,990 --> 00:07:18,650
I'll be honest,

273
00:07:18,650 --> 00:07:20,610
nothing dramatic had
happened.

274
00:07:20,610 --> 00:07:22,180
And after what that video
said,

275
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:24,320
that's exactly what I
expected.

276
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:25,130
What was different

277
00:07:25,130 --> 00:07:26,360
was that for the first

278
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:27,800
time in two years

279
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:29,740
I'd done something for my
knee

280
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:31,280
instead of to it.

281
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:32,260
Twenty minutes,

282
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:33,640
in my own chair.

283
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:35,290
No drive, no copay.

284
00:07:35,290 --> 00:07:36,860
They say twenty minutes.

285
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:38,090
I did thirty,

286
00:07:38,090 --> 00:07:39,350
twice a day,

287
00:07:39,350 --> 00:07:41,490
lowest setting that first
week.

288
00:07:41,490 --> 00:07:42,840
I put it on the calendar.

289
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:43,890
The first week,

290
00:07:43,890 --> 00:07:44,740
I couldn't have told

291
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:46,340
you if anything was
happening.

292
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:47,210
I tried not to get

293
00:07:47,210 --> 00:07:48,170
my hopes up.

294
00:07:48,170 --> 00:07:49,540
I'd had things help for a
week

295
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:50,980
and then stop.

296
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:52,420
But somewhere in the
second week

297
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:53,640
I noticed I'd come down

298
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:55,670
the stairs without holding
the rail.

299
00:07:55,670 --> 00:07:56,820
I hadn't decided to.

300
00:07:56,820 --> 00:07:58,060
I just did it,

301
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:59,620
then stopped halfway down

302
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:01,160
because I realized.

303
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,590
By the end of the fourth
week

304
00:08:02,590 --> 00:08:03,660
I'd slept through the
night

305
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:05,270
four times running.

306
00:08:05,270 --> 00:08:06,270
I stood at the counter

307
00:08:06,270 --> 00:08:07,360
and finished making dinner

308
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:09,260
